      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [X] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\n- [X] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\n- [X] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a feature request that matches the one I want to file, without success.\n\n### Problem Description\n\nSFSymbols are macOS native icons consisting of 3k+ high quality icons. Currently seems there is no way to use them in Electron apps built for macOS.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"691\" alt=\"CleanShot 2022-09-16 at 21 47 10@2x\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7311462/190718766-6c6e1fe0-3407-44f5-b1f4-13ca7645f8c8.png\">\r\n\r\nIt is trivial to use it natively in swiftUI\r\n\r\n```swift\r\nImage(systemName: \"square.and.pencil\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n\n\n### Proposed Solution\n\neg.\r\n\r\n```ts\r\nnativeImage.fromSFSymbolName(\"square.and.pencil\")\r\n```\n\n### Alternatives Considered\n\nIt is possible to export SFSymbols to PNG using native MacOS app \"SF Symbols\", but it is quite a manual process.\n\n### Additional Information\n\n_No response_",
